# Python in this repo

Agent and shell commands do not load interactive zsh/conda by default. Do not assume bare `python` exists on PATH.

This repo has no `environment.yml`. Use the env documented in the README or ask the user before assuming a conda env name.

The user activates it with:

```bash
source utils/venv
```

For agent-driven commands, use that env explicitly:

If you add `environment.yml`, read the `name:` field and use:

```bash
conda run -n <name> python -m scripts.<module> …
```

Run scripts as packages: `python -m scripts.<module>` (from repo root, with the env above).
